	<key>readme</key>
	<string># 🎩 Alfred Dashlane

✨ *Search your Dashlane vault from Alfred* ✨

## ✅ Prerequisites

* macOS, Alfred 5 with the [Powerpack](https://www.alfredapp.com/powerpack/).
* A [Dashlane](https://www.dashlane.com) account with a master password.
* **Python 3.9** or above (`python3 --version`).
* The [Dashlane CLI](https://dashlane.github.io/dashlane-cli/install) (`dcli`), for example `brew install dashlane/tap/dashlane-cli`.

## 🧰 Setup

1. Fill `👤 Login` with your Dashlane email.
2. Type `pdash` and press ⏎ on **Login to Dashlane**: a Dashlane page opens in your browser. Paste the token it shows, then the 6-digit code (email or authenticator app), then your master password in the hidden macOS dialog.

## 🧙‍♂️ Usage

* `pdash`: passwords. `odash`: OTP codes.
* ⏎ copy password (or OTP) · ⌘⏎ copy login · ⌥⏎ open URL · ⇧⏎ type login ⇥ password in the frontmost app · ⌃⏎ copy OTP.
* Sync, Lock, Devices, Download favicons, Clear cache and Logout always stay at the top of the list, in this order.
* Results come as native macOS notifications (`🔔 Notifications`), or on the first line of the list when notifications are off.
* Works with Alfred 5 and Alfred 6; with Alfred 6, unsupported modifier combinations do nothing (`strictmods`) and favicons keep their proportions.

## 🔐 Security

* Master password, token and codes are typed in native macOS dialogs (hidden for the password) and sent to dcli through its terminal: never in Alfred's bar, a command line or an environment variable.
* No password or OTP secret is ever written to disk. The optional list cache holds titles, URLs and logins only, exists only while dcli is unlocked and is deleted as soon as the vault locks.
* Copied secrets are marked transient (kept out of clipboard history) and erased after the delay you choose.

Full documentation on [GitHub](https://github.com/BenjaminOddou/alfred-dashlane).

© Benjamin Oddou</string>
